I wrote two task files for this session and an issue-responses file. The plan isn't committed: session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so the commit command didn't add anything. The files are on disk, which should be enough if the harness reads them from there.

• Task 1 (Part of #1122): use yoagent 0.27.3's temperature flag (product). Today yoyo works out for itself which Claude versions reject temperature, and only for anthropic and bedrock. yoagent now drops temperature for OpenRouter anthropic/claude-* ids too, so an OpenRouter user who passes --temperature loses it and yoyo says nothing. The task does what @yuanhao asked on #1146: read config.accepts_sampling_params and keep the stderr note when the flag is off.
  • The test table includes the OpenRouter row, which should fail before the change and pass after.
  • It covers his three limits: gateway and custom configs, configs rebuilt by /model, and configs saved before 0.27.3.
  • If yoagent doesn't publicly expose its id-to-flag rule, the task posts a short request upstream rather than writing a second copy of the version check.

• Task 2 (Fixes #1150): refuse stray words with `-p` (product). yoyo -p hi extra sends only hi and drops extra without saying so. Since fb0c95bf it also drops claude-zzz in the #1114 example. The fix refuses the run with exit 2 and "Nothing ran", the same way an unknown flag is already refused (#1109). Words after -- keep working.
  • The task first tries each input shape on the built binary, because the ticket was written from reading code and nobody has run it yet.
  • It then checks every yoyo call in scripts/ and .github/. If any of my own loop's calls would be refused, it switches to a warning.
  • The check goes in cli_config.rs. cli.rs is already at its recorded size, so it only gets the call site.
  • tests/flag_value_slot.rs currently asserts that the "Unknown model" line is absent; that assertion changes to expect the new refusal.

